m=read('metrics.json');lat=m['latency'];now=datetime.now(timezone(timedelta(hours=-5)));archive=R/'handoff'/f'CURRENT_REVIEW({now:%Y%m%d-%H%M%S}).zip'
headline=f"B — PARTIAL / DYNAMIC NPC PATHWAY DEMONSTRATED. Six live provider NPC proposals were validated and committed across the retained runs; four NPCs completed final HTTP/browser lifecycle verification. The first two live HTTP NPCs persisted but their resumed references clarified incorrectly. Final HTTP A/B and browser A/B pass after the target-gate repair. All 150 protected files match. Twelve live requests, 3,398 tokens, zero retries. All six sampled live dialogue rewordings were rejected; grounded host fallbacks carried conversation. This is bounded conversational functionality, not demonstrated broad AI dialogue competence. No commit or push."
architecture='''Player input → existing `player_initiative.decide` → `bounded_improvisation.controlled_request` (read-only) → existing ELABORATE interpretation record → `player_interpretation_bridge` revalidation → existing exploration resolver → proposal/identity validation → accepted entry in the existing bounded ledger → API runtime transaction/save → resolver-owned publication → existing player HTTP projection. Dialogue selects identity/public context/previous validated speech, then reuses `expressive_dialogue.build_expression_contract`, `request_expression`, and `validate_expression`. Memory stays under `conversational_context.dialogue_commitments`, capped at eight exchanges per NPC and 24 overall. Social receipts remain on the same accepted NPC record. Normal storage/snapshots restore everything together. There is no new database, provider abstraction, dialogue engine, frontend framework or persistence backend.

Authored NPC records remain in the existing world roster and keep priority. Accepted background NPCs are authoritative runtime identities in the existing ledger, rather than authored-world replacements. Stable IDs bind campaign plus scene. One new background identity per scene is the explicit bounded policy. Rejected proposals are private diagnostics; narration alone never creates identities.'''
limitations='\n'.join('- '+x for x in m['limitations'])+'''\n- The proposal chooses an ordinary role from six engine-approved roles. It may choose a different ordinary role than the player's descriptive request; the committed role is then stable. This remains a product limitation.
- Compound conversation is shallow: browser "Hello. Who are you?" returned a greeting only. Single-purpose identity questions and follow-ups work.
- Actual provider admission IDs, returned proposals, model/usage and latency are captured. Exact provider wire request bodies were not captured; public-only prompt construction remains inspectable in source. No reconstructed payload is represented as a wire capture.
- No official ATGB scoring, authenticated human review, independent external holdout, full-suite green claim, NPC autonomy, quest generation or PR-PLAY-76 implementation.'''
sections=[
('01_EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY',headline+'\n\n'+limitations+'\n\nReview archive: `'+str(archive)+'`. Machine summary: `artifacts/pr_play_75/metrics.json`.'),
('02_REPOSITORY_BASELINE','Branch: `feature/product-realization`. Revision: `d40f1ed198236c604085f1c842ead267a8104ce2`. Extensive dirty/untracked state predates this task. `baseline.json` records entry status; `source_before/` retains entry bytes. `source_task.diff` separates this task from pre-existing edits. Runtime changes: game/api.py, game/bounded_improvisation.py, game/dialogue_authority.py, game/expressive_dialogue.py. New tests: test_pr_play_75_dynamic_npcs.py and test_pr_play_75_persistence.py. Also changed NEXT_SESSION and generated this cycle evidence/review exports. PR74 tests, frozen files and protected data were not edited.'),
('03_TEST_DATA_ISOLATION','150/150 entry protected hashes preserved. The inherited 150-path manifest was re-hashed before implementation. Existing storage_isolation.install runs before game imports. Separate roots cover development, holdout, HTTP, browser, faults, provider logs, save slots, performance and reports. Its audit guard rejects production-data and historical-artifact writes. HTTP helper import initially reset provider flags; the corrected harness restores only budgeted NPC lanes. Reusing an old usage log was refused safely; final HTTP uses http_final_data. No production data was restored or overwritten. Initial failures/evidence remain retained.'),
('04_NPC_ARCHITECTURE',architecture),
('05_DYNAMIC_NPC_CREATION','Creation requires explicit introduction intent, feature enrollment, matching current campaign/scene and affirmative public population support. Empty/deserted/abandoned/inaccessible/no-people contexts reject. Old Milestone cannot be populated just for the test; campaigns return to the existing gate crowd. Harbor/quay fixtures demonstrate vocabulary independent of Cinderwatch and stone. The provider proposes structured name/role/appearance/demeanor; engine code creates identity, location, label, provenance, creation turn and interaction scope. Extra fields and consequential attributes fail closed. Six ordinary roles and four clothing choices are deliberate current limits.'),
('06_NPC_AUTHORITY_AND_PROVENANCE','Accepted identities live in bounded_improvisation.entries with authority=accepted_background_npc, provenance=accepted_improvisation, source=validated_provider_proposal, public visibility, campaign/scene binding and stable hash ID. Existing authored names are preserved. Repeated descriptions reuse the existing identity. Raw/rejected proposals stay in private bounded diagnostics, with at most 24 rejection receipts. Temporary prose is not a record. Authored roster entries are not overwritten. `npc_identity_records.json` and `live_provider_proposals.json` preserve all six real committed identities.'),
('07_LIVE_PROVIDER_PROPOSALS','12 actual requests / 3,398 measured tokens / 0 retries. Six proposal requests produced six accepted and committed NPCs, zero rejected live proposals; four final HTTP/browser identities have complete lifecycle verification. Six other requests attempted conversational wording. Initial offline and accounting-refusal attempts made zero live dispatches and remain separate evidence. Existing OpenAI configuration, SDK retry policy and provider_budget admission/accounting are reused. Single proposal attempt; a timeout/malformed proposal cannot publish an NPC. No fixture is counted as live.'),
('08_NATURAL_CONVERSATION','Reusable conversation accepts greetings, identity/local questions, uncertainty, thanks and contextual follow-ups using current focus or grounded references. Host meaning comes from accepted identity, one public population anchor or previous validated speech. No exact input phrase is required, and no per-NPC dialogue tree was authored. However semantic breadth is narrow and compound requests can be under-answered. All sampled provider rewordings failed validation and used grounded fallback lines, so broad provider-led conversation is unproven. This is a principal reason for B/PARTIAL.'),
('09_NPC_KNOWLEDGE_BOUNDARIES','NPC view contains accepted identity/role/location, public population support and relevant validated speech. Hidden GM facts, undiscovered clues, branch flags and unrestricted world state are not supplied to the dialogue provider. Questions do not become knowledge. Unestablished road history receives uncertainty. Quest, treasure, secret-passage, noble/faction authority and unsupported assistance requests do not gain facts or effects. Browser B shows a grounded refusal and continued conversation. Host-selected public facts are shared local context; no NPC-specific plot knowledge was added.'),
('10_CONVERSATIONAL_MEMORY','Existing conversational_context.dialogue_commitments stores campaign, player/session identity, NPC ID, turn, original utterance, published response and modest social receipt. Eight exchanges per NPC / 24 overall; duplicate same-turn receipt is idempotent. History is not world truth. Ephemeral phrasing remains transcript memory; this cycle does not promote additional biographies or freeform facts. Prior delivered speech supplies contextual explanations. Final tests and browser/HTTP traces verify restored history plus a fresh same-NPC response after loading.'),
('11_SOCIAL_CONSEQUENCES','Only unique greeted/thanked receipts are persisted. They record prior interaction without trust, allegiance, faction reputation, compliance, quests, treasure or promises. Existing authored social mechanics remain authoritative. Dynamic background NPC persuasion/bribery/intimidation/combat attempts report that established mechanics are required; this cycle does not fabricate checks or social statistics. This remains a functional limitation. Normal conversation consumes a transcript turn but preserves faction/world and time-pressure clocks.'),
('12_ROUTINE_INTERACTION_POLICY','A narrow reusable policy recognizes sitting on an accepted, accessible ordinary seat in the active scene. It requires no roll or invented DC. Missing/imaginary/inaccessible seats do not gain success. The result is a scene-scoped posture receipt in the existing ledger, without inventory or movement effects; repeated sitting does not duplicate entities/effects. Seat improvisation itself retains PR74 public stone support. Final HTTP campaigns create the seat at the milestone and return to the gate afterward. Pickup, movement, climbing and broader physical adjudication remain deferred to PR76.'),
('13_REFERENCE_AND_IDENTITY','Public name, role, canonical label and contextual/pronoun references resolve the same campaign-scene identity. Name matches now require word boundaries, preventing Eli from matching believe. Current focus cannot expose another scene/campaign; stale scene envelopes reject. Multiple plausible background identities clarify without mutation; absent references do not create a replacement. The initial live HTTP run exposed a duplicate authored-roster gate: stable NPCs survived load, but resumed references clarified. API now skips only that duplicate gate after bridge acceptance and exact target revalidation. Stronger final tests assert a new memory exchange, not merely identity survival.'),
('14_CONTRADICTION_AND_ESCALATION','Strict proposal shape rejects hidden, authority, effects, inventories and biography fields. Dialogue reuses existing expression validation plus ordered predicate/polarity preservation for factual paraphrases. Hostile negations, subject reversals, secret/quest/treasure/authority claims and unsupported promises are rejected. Unknown provider failures use grounded fallback, without raw internal errors. The frozen holdout was not tuned or rerun. Development repairs address memory bucket ownership, ordinary-turn ticks, duplicate target grounding, player-information ownership and name boundaries.'),
('15_PERSISTENCE_AND_RESUME','Normal storage and snapshots persist identity, knowledge scope, memory and social receipts together. Final HTTP A/B and browser A/B save, reload/load and append a fresh response from the same ID. Browser cross-loads preserve distinct campaigns and branches. The frozen developer holdout exercised 20 real snapshot lifecycles, but its resumed-conversation assertion was weaker than the repaired final development checks. Two NPC-specific commit fault tests force creation/dialogue writes to fail; all prior session/world/combat/transcript bytes remain unchanged and no NPC speech is published. Existing Windows transient/permanent rename tests remain green.'),
('16_PLAYER_SAFE_PUBLICATION','Existing resolver-owned engine_publication and allowlisted player HTTP DTOs publish committed appearance and validated speech only. NPC diagnostics, raw proposals, prompt contracts, flags and relationship metadata remain private. Complete exercised serialized HTTP/browser responses were scanned for sentinels and internal keys. Known mandatory notice and milestone discoveries were checked. Zero observed hidden exposures, disclosure omissions or critical unsafe publications in that scope. This is not a proof of unrestricted prose safety. Package authority snapshots redact campaign GM-only fields; original player inputs and player-facing responses remain intact.'),
('17_DEVELOPMENT_TESTS','Final NPC lane: 70/70. Final broader safety slice: 234/234 (overlapping coverage, not additive). Inherited PR73/authority lane: 105/105, comprising a 100-case run and the five existing bounded-authority checks. NPC fault lane: 3/3 before the added alias test, with all four persistence/reference checks included in final 70. Initial 46/55 exposed nine memory ownership failures; initial 60/61 exposed routine world ticking. Retain these development logs. Tests assert hostile schema, scene support, deduplication, authored preservation, hidden boundaries, unsafe dialogue, polarity, idempotent memory, read-only inquiry, stale scene, routine accessibility and normal lifecycle.'),
('18_FROZEN_HOLDOUT','Frozen before implementation: 90 cases, hash `61173fbd9a629c59f38b6a37404c1f68421a10204af886112452920679729113`. Single run: 85 passed / 5 failed; 30 multi-turn sequences and 20 actual save/resume cases. H66/H68/H70/H72/H74 raise KeyError(skill_check) after routine resolution succeeds because to_dict omits null optional fields. These failures are preserved, not reclassified as PASS or tuned away. The manifest uses broad developer-authored assertions; resumed dialogue checks proved too weak and were strengthened only in development/HTTP/browser verification. The run source predates later target/inquiry/name refinements. No final-source holdout or external independent validation is claimed.'),
('19_REAL_HTTP_GAMEPLAY','Final normal TCP campaigns A/survey and B/report both PASS. New Campaign → Start → notice → milestone → exclusive branch/follow-up → suitable populated gate → live NPC proposal/validation/commit/publication → conversation → routine seat at milestone → save → fresh campaign → load → restored transcript/history → same-NPC response. Two final live proposal calls / 703 tokens; dialogue in this final rerun uses host fallback after the earlier live wording sample. Full original requests, publications, stage timings and authority before/after are retained. Initial live HTTP continuation was partial and remains separate. A third bounded attempt refused old accounting state with zero dispatches; final fresh-root run is distinct.'),
('20_BROWSER_GAMEPLAY',f"Two normal typed browser campaigns PASS, {m['browser']['typed_submissions']} chat submissions. Campaign A: survey, live Mira creation, greeting, identity, contextual follow-up, snapshot/reload/load, same-NPC reply. Campaign B: report, live Eli creation, greeting, unknown road history, secret-passage/quest refusal, snapshot/reload/load, continued uncertainty. Both additionally cross-loaded and continued on hash-recorded final source with provider calls disabled. Player inquiry on A preserved all authoritative domains. Screenshots and middleware network traces retained. Intermittent input/locator deadlines were recovered by inspecting state, without replaying already-submitted actions. Browser paint timing unavailable."),
('21_REGRESSION_RESULTS','Focused 1,065 passed / 20 failed; boundary 101 / 6; broader authority 0 / 9; isolated lifecycle 39 / 0. Exact failure identities match PR74; new failures 0. The combined regression source precedes late narrowly scoped target/inquiry/name guards; final safety/NPC/authority lanes and both browser continuations cover those final changes. No full-suite claim. `regression_comparison.json` records exact identity differences, rather than inferring history from counts.'),
('22_LATENCY_AND_PROVIDER_USAGE','Actual measurements (milliseconds):\n\n```json\n'+json.dumps(lat,indent=2)+'\n```\n\nFinal conversation timing includes HTTP/persistence while several isolated validation processes ran concurrently; it is not a controlled load-free benchmark. Provider 12 requests / 3,398 tokens / 0 retries. Proposal acceptance 6/6. Sampled live dialogue adoption 0/6. Separate validation/authored-NPC microbenchmarks are in performance_supplement.json; authored narration uses an offline fixture. Atomic-write and resolver substage timing is captured, but separate NPC commit/publication latency and browser paint time are unavailable.'),
('23_LIMITATIONS_AND_OPEN_RISKS',limitations),
('24_NEXT_SESSION','Proceed toward PR-PLAY-76 — GENERAL-PURPOSE ACTION ADJUDICATION AND ENVIRONMENTAL INTERACTION. Safe dynamic identities persist, bounded conversation works, and remaining gaps are noncritical. Preserve authority and isolation; do not implement PR76 in this cycle or rerun/tune this frozen holdout. Do not create another stabilization cycle solely for shallow personalities, repeated phrasing, historical failures or unavailable paint timing. Read 01/04/13/18/23, metrics.json, source_task.diff, final_source.json, final browser/HTTP results and exact regression comparison. No commit or push without authorization.')]
